Nokia's copyright notice.

FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org), LGPL 2.1 or later (LICENSES/LGPL-2.1.txt)
  Fetched at build time and configured without --enable-gpl, --enable-version3 or --enable-nonfree; the recipe asserts
  the configure licence line. It is built as the separate, replaceable DLL pheffmpeg.dll (and the AAC decoder
  library), never statically linked into an EPL component, so users can relink or replace it: the LGPL condition.

OpenH264 (https://github.com/cisco/openh264), Copyright (c) 2013, Cisco Systems, BSD-2-Clause
  (LICENSES/BSD-2-Clause-OpenH264.txt). Built from source here. Cisco's patent licence for H.264 covers only the
  binaries Cisco itself distributes, not a build from source.

Patents: AAC and H.264 are patent-grey in many jurisdictions. This pack is distributed as source plus build
instructions only. It is not part of any Phorepoc image; users install a build of it themselves, through the download
app, and are responsible for any licences their use needs.

Thanks to the FFmpeg and OpenH264 projects.
